{ ==========================================================================
  IND_S16S_P29  --  broadening formation detector (P29 / P49 / P50)

  Build_ID 260893.  DETECTION ONLY.  Places no orders, holds no position.

  ACCEPTED IN MC12, 2026-08-31, build 260881.  Every line of the acceptance
  table matched, on a chart of 421,455 bars starting 2019-01-02 13:40:

    bars 421,455   pivot_high 75,136   pivot_low 76,017
    formations 202   P49 112   P50 90   by_year 8 15 18 31 24 31 42 33
    P29 202  P51 1670  P52 1715  P53 7  P54 8
    P52 by_year 94 172 229 267 169 258 302 224
    REV   P18 6352   P57 255   P68 1367
    CUP   P28 7   P64 4   P55 628
    DIA   P30 0   P61 1
    break_down 75   break_up 88   expired 39   slot_overflow 0
    sum = formations on all three LIFE lines

  THE VERDICT, and it is negative
    P18  dn 2190  up 2153   50.43%   z +0.56
    P57  dn  105  up   89   54.12%   z +1.15
    P68  dn  538  up  466   53.59%   z +2.27
    P29  dn   75  up   88   46.01%   z -1.02   (control)

    These three were selected out of 72 shapes on their mirror ratios
    (P18 10.19x, P68 6.75x, P57 2.33x), so the threshold that applies is the
    one for the whole search, not for three tests: this project already set
    2.96 for its 33 tests, and 72 shapes would need 3.20.  P68's 2.27 does
    not reach it, and P18 -- the strongest candidate by mirror ratio -- is a
    coin flip at 50.43%.

    Per the rule written down on 2026-08-30 BEFORE the numbers existed:
    dn ~ up means break direction carries no pattern information.  The
    "shapes with a direction" leg of the pattern layer is empty.  What is
    NOT killed: P64's price band (untested, and 4 instances in eight years
    is unlikely to carry a test), and the primitives -- the 2x2 of
    higher-highs by higher-lows, the band device, slope comparison, the
    decay law -- which describe rather than predict.

  Build history, the reasoning behind every rule, and the measurement
  each one rests on:  docs/research/S16S_P29_comment_record.md
  ======================================================================== }

inputs:
    Build_ID                ( 260893 ),
    M7_Bars                 ( 12    ),     { ruling 11.  PINNED.  Never sweep. }

    { 260870, ruling X3 of 2026-08-28 -- record }
    Pivot_Window            ( 1     ),
    Run_Bars                ( 3     ),     { ruling 18.  PINNED.  Never sweep. }
    Sess_Day_Start          ( 845   ),
    Sess_Day_End            ( 1345  ),
    Sess_Night_Start        ( 1500  ),
    Sess_Night_End          ( 500   ),
    Line_Mode               ( 1     ),     { 0 off, 1 trendline objects, 2 legacy Plot }
    Print_Events            ( 1     ),     { emit one line per event for diff }
    Log_Lines               ( 0     ),     { 1 = log every TL_New and TL_SetEnd -- record }
    Show_State              ( 0     ),     { 0 = off.  Plot5 shares the price axis. }
    Show_Pivots             ( 0     ),     { 0 = off.  See the note at SECTION 8. }
    Col_Upper               ( Red       ),
    Col_Lower               ( LightGray ), { Cyan until 260840, Green in 260840 -- record }
    Line_Width              ( 3     ),
    Paint_Mode              ( 1     ),     { 0 off, 1 recolour the pattern's own bars }
    Col_Active              ( Blue    ),   { state 1, alive and waiting -- record }
    Col_Testing             ( Magenta ),   { state 2, price is testing an edge }
    Col_Shape_Top           ( Yellow  ),   { P49 broadening TOP, prior trend up }
    Col_Shape_Bot           ( Cyan    ),   { P50 broadening BOTTOM, prior down -- record }
    Paint_MaxBack           ( 60      ),   { cap on the back-paint.  Longest span
                                             measured is 43; CLAUDE.md allows 99 }

    { ruling C, 2026-08-27 -- record }
    { broadening family, 2026-08-28 -- record }
    Enable_P29              ( 1       ),   { 202.  highs rise, lows fall }
    Enable_P51              ( 1       ),   { 1,670.  both rise, highs faster }
    Enable_P52              ( 1       ),   { 1,716.  both fall, lows faster }
    Enable_P53              ( 1       ),   { 7.  flat top, lows fall }
    Enable_P54              ( 1       ),   { 8.  highs rise, flat bottom }
    Col_Shape_P51           ( DarkGreen ),
    Col_Shape_P52           ( DarkRed   ),
    Col_Shape_P53           ( DarkCyan  ),
    Col_Shape_P54           ( DarkBrown ),

    { P30 / P61 diamond, ruling I1 of 2026-08-28 -- record }
    Enable_P30              ( 1       ),   { diamond TOP,    prior trend up }
    Enable_P61              ( 1       ),   { diamond BOTTOM, prior trend down }
    Col_Shape_P30           ( DarkMagenta ),
    Col_Shape_P61           ( DarkBlue    ),
    Col_Dia_Line            ( Magenta     ),  { the four edges -- record }
    Dia_Line_Width          ( 2       ),

    Break_Mode              ( 1       ),   { 0 off, 1 track and paint breaks }
    Col_Break               ( White   ),   { the bar that closes below the floor }
    Col_BreakUp             ( Green   ),   { closes above the ceiling -- record }
    Show_Labels             ( 1       ),   { 0 off.  one label per formation, one
                                             per break, sharing a sequence number }
    Label_Size              ( 8       ),
    Label_Offset_Pct        ( 6       ),

    { 260870 -- record }
    Enable_P18              ( 1       ),   { triple top, band device, 10.19x }
    Enable_P57              ( 1       ),   { measured move down, 2.33x }
    Enable_P68              ( 1       ),   { double top, 6.75x }
    Col_Revisit             ( LightGray ),  { labels only -- see below }

    { 260880.  Ruling A1: the cup is drawn to be SEEN, not traded -- 7 in eight
      years, 4 for the mirror.  What is drawn is the RIM BAND, because a band
      is a price and an outline is only a shape. -- record }
    Enable_P28              ( 1       ),   { cup and handle, 7 }
    Enable_P64              ( 1       ),   { inverted cup and handle, 4 }
    Enable_P55              ( 1       ),   { bump-and-run, 628 }
    Col_Cup                 ( Yellow  ),   { the two rims }
    { ---- SECTION 6e, the seven whose logic was already reviewed ----------
      2026-08-31 ruling: the pattern layer lands when a shape that OCCURS is
      drawn, not when it tests.  These seven have zero-parameter definitions,
      per-condition logic and real bar cases, and all seven carry Willy's
      ruling.  Definitions transcribed unchanged from
        s16s_census15_scan.py   P26 P32 P56 P59 P65 P72
        s16s_hs_scan.py         P15  (the loose form -- shoulder symmetry
                                would need a tolerance, so it is not used)

      P15 was ruled DO-NOT-CODE on 08-29, on the grounds that the mirror passes
      too and so it carries no direction.  That was the OLD standard.  The
      08-31 standard is "a shape that happened gets drawn", exactly as P51
      and P52 were reinstated on 08-28.  Superseded, and recorded as such.

      The counts are large and that is a fact, not a reason to hide them:
        P72 18,705   P56 9,134   P65 8,572   P15 5,242
        P59    309   P32    97   P26    60          total 42,119
      Drawing rides on the file's existing Show_Labels and Line_Mode
      switches, so the capacity decision stays where the other patterns'
      already is rather than becoming seven private defaults. ---- }
    Enable_P15              ( 1       ),   { head and shoulders, 5,242 }
    Enable_P26              ( 1       ),   { rounding top, 60 }
    Enable_P32              ( 1       ),   { V reversal, 97 }
    Enable_P56              ( 1       ),   { dead-cat bounce, 9,134 }
    Enable_P59              ( 1       ),   { descending scallop, 309 }
    Enable_P65              ( 1       ),   { tower top, 8,572 }
    Enable_P72              ( 1       ),   { order block, 18,705 }
    Col_P15                 ( Magenta   ),
    Col_P26                 ( DarkGray  ),
    Col_P32                 ( Red       ),
    Col_P56                 ( Green     ),
    Col_P59                 ( Blue      ),
    Col_P65                 ( LightGray ),
    Col_P72                 ( Cyan      ),
    Col_Bump                ( Magenta );   { the lead-in line }   { display nudge only, as a percentage of
                                             the formation's own height -- self
                                             referential, so not a magic distance }

